<section class="wrap" style="max-width:70ch;">
  <p style="margin:0 0 28px;"><img src="/assets/ui/koa-gully-boat.webp" alt="Koa waving on the beach while Gully wrestles the boat's mooring rope" style="width:100%;border-radius:var(--radius-lg);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card);display:block;"></p>
  <p>Koa's Beach Adventures began with a simple idea: children learn best when they don't feel like they're learning at all. When a story carries them somewhere real — a beach they could one day stand on, an animal that actually lives there — the facts stop being facts. They become part of an adventure a child was already having.</p>

  <p>So every book follows the same promise. Koa arrives somewhere new. He meets a local friend who knows that place better than anyone. Together they discover what makes it special — and together they leave it a little better than they found it. The local friend teaches Koa about their home; Koa shares what he knows about caring for the world. Nobody lectures. Nobody knows everything. Learning is always shared.</p>

  <p>Every adventure weaves together the same five threads:</p>
  <ul style="line-height:1.9;">
    <li><strong>Wildlife</strong> — real animals, drawn with love, worth meeting.</li>
    <li><strong>Culture</strong> — real communities, treated with respect and curiosity.</li>
    <li><strong>Geography</strong> — real places a child can find on a map and dream of visiting.</li>
    <li><strong>Friendship</strong> — because no adventure is worth having alone.</li>
    <li><strong>Care for nature</strong> — always through hope and action, never guilt or fear.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>The world in these books is something wonderful to discover and look after — and we think children who grow up believing that will do exactly both.</p>

